Premiums will increase in future

00:05:56.624 --> 00:06:00.918
Now, why do I think this is the best time for you
to purchase life and term insurance both?

00:06:00.943 --> 00:06:04.253
1. The first one is quite logical,
that 'Disasters do not occur with prior warning.'

00:06:04.278 --> 00:06:05.928
What If something happens tomorrow?

00:06:05.953 --> 00:06:07.352
What were you waiting for?

00:06:07.377 --> 00:06:08.710
Stating that you will purchase the policy later.

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:11.061
No, you must purchase it today.
It's as simple as that.

00:06:11.086 --> 00:06:13.522
The second answer is that insurance is related to business.

00:06:13.522 --> 00:06:16.105
For that you need to understand, 'Input Tax Credit'.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:17.648
Now, GST is a 'Sales Tax'.

00:06:17.673 --> 00:06:19.204
Whenever the company does a sale,

00:06:19.229 --> 00:06:20.970
they charge GST from the customer..

00:06:20.995 --> 00:06:23.383
and then proceed to pay the GST to the government.

00:06:23.408 --> 00:06:25.164
But the company doesn't just sell.

00:06:25.189 --> 00:06:27.436
It also purchases, i.e. they also incur expenses.

00:06:27.461 --> 00:06:29.968
The company has to pay GST on those expenses too.

00:06:29.993 --> 00:06:32.242
What are the type of expenses in an insurance business?

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:35.396
Agent commission, office rent, professional services,

00:06:35.431 --> 00:06:38.476
office equipment such as laptop, TV, AC, sofa, etc.

00:06:38.501 --> 00:06:39.540
So let's understand this with an example.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:42.948
Presume that the insurance company
did a sale of ₹5,000 crore.

00:06:42.973 --> 00:06:45.307
It means they received a premium costing ₹5,000 crores.

00:06:45.307 --> 00:06:47.365
But there is an 18% GST levied on it too.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:50.063
Hence, the gross sales have been drawn as ₹5,900 crores.

00:06:50.088 --> 00:06:53.809
And in the past one year, the insurance company
has incurred ₹1,000 crore in expenses.

00:06:53.834 --> 00:06:57.530
On that, 18% GST, i.e. they have paid ₹180 crore GST.

00:06:57.555 --> 00:07:00.017
Now this sales GST, i.e. ₹900 crore..

00:07:00.042 --> 00:07:03.106
which they have charged customers along with the insurance premium.

00:07:03.131 --> 00:07:06.628
The company's responsibility is to deposit
 this ₹900 crore to the government.

00:07:06.653 --> 00:07:10.057
But the government offers a benefit
which is known as 'Input Tax Credit'.

00:07:10.082 --> 00:07:11.179
What it means is,

00:07:11.204 --> 00:07:14.906
The GST collected by you at the time of sales
 amounting to ₹900 crores.

00:07:14.931 --> 00:07:16.255
While deposting the same.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:22.282
You can deduct the already paid
GST of ₹180 crore at the time of expenses.

00:07:22.307 --> 00:07:26.259
Now this company will pay
₹720 crores as Net GST to the government.

00:07:26.284 --> 00:07:29.421
And they will receive the Input Tax Credit of ₹180 crores.

00:07:29.446 --> 00:07:30.597
So their profit would be..

00:07:30.622 --> 00:07:37.627
Gross Revenue, i.e. ₹5,900 crores - Cost i.e. ₹1,180 crores - ₹720 crore,
which is paid to the government.

00:07:37.652 --> 00:07:38.779
What's left is ₹4,000 crores.

00:07:38.804 --> 00:07:43.591
Now, If it's not allowed to charge GST
on sales of upto ₹5,000 crores.

00:07:43.616 --> 00:07:45.008
which means If you are not receiving those ₹900 crores.

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:47.869
The company doesn't owe the government anything.

00:07:47.894 --> 00:07:49.211
There is no need to deposit any GST.

00:07:49.236 --> 00:07:54.295
And If there is no need to deposit GST,
then ₹180 crores paid in the form of expenses.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.724
How will you claim that?

00:07:55.749 --> 00:07:57.521
In such a case, the company's equation will change.

00:07:57.521 --> 00:08:02.153
On the ₹5,000 crore revenue,
they will have to subtract the cost of ₹1,180 crore..

00:08:02.178 --> 00:08:05.273
and their profit would be ₹3,820 crore.

00:08:05.298 --> 00:08:07.273
It means, if you don't receive input tax credit,

00:08:07.273 --> 00:08:10.235
then the company's cost will increase by 18%.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.917
Now, tell me this..

00:08:11.942 --> 00:08:14.135
Are companies charitable organisations?

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.459
Will they keep providing you with services
at a higher cost of 18%..

00:08:17.484 --> 00:08:20.127
Will they keep selling insurance
and won't increase the premiums?

00:08:20.152 --> 00:08:22.081
If you were a shareholder of such a company,

00:08:22.106 --> 00:08:23.542
would you have been happy with this decision?

00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:27.541
"Our investment is worth ₹35 lakhs,
then how did we incur a loss of ₹36 lakhs?"

00:08:27.566 --> 00:08:28.415
Now I am not trying to scare you.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.766
I am not saying that the premiums will increase by 18%.

00:08:30.791 --> 00:08:31.839
In fact, the opposite is happening.

00:08:31.864 --> 00:08:35.191
A minimum deduction of 10% to 15%
has been imposed from today onwards.

00:08:35.216 --> 00:08:37.693
It's happening based on the assumption
that insurance adoption would increase.

00:08:37.718 --> 00:08:40.496
More people will be able to afford insurance policies.

00:08:40.521 --> 00:08:44.018
The higher cost will be offset by higher sales volume.

00:08:44.043 --> 00:08:48.049
And the biggest advantage of GST deduction
will reflect in term and health insurance policies.

00:08:48.074 --> 00:08:49.846
Because these are pure risk policies.

00:08:49.871 --> 00:08:52.610
The companies don't have to pay anything
until there is a claim request.

00:08:52.635 --> 00:08:56.084
Whereas, the other life insurance policies,
which has 'investment components'..

00:08:56.109 --> 00:08:59.014
such as Money Back, Guaranteed Income or ULIP plans.

00:08:59.039 --> 00:09:00.896
There is a maturity value in this..

00:09:00.921 --> 00:09:03.493
It's a huge amount,
which the company has to pay.

00:09:03.518 --> 00:09:07.378
In such plans, to pass on the entire benefit
of GST deduction to customers,

00:09:07.403 --> 00:09:08.920
doesn't seem like a sensible option.

00:09:08.945 --> 00:09:09.736
But why should we care?

00:09:09.761 --> 00:09:13.542
We have always told that term and health insurance
 are the most important insurances.

00:09:13.567 --> 00:09:15.484
And you will be receiving a benefit on that.

00:09:15.484 --> 00:09:18.681
But this benefit will keep reducing gradually.

00:09:18.706 --> 00:09:21.232
Due to the absence of input tax credit.

00:09:21.257 --> 00:09:23.330
So my suggestion for you is to purchase term insurance..

00:09:23.355 --> 00:09:25.534
and lock the cheapest premium today.

00:09:25.566 --> 00:09:26.988
Because they will be same for your lifetime.

00:09:27.013 --> 00:09:29.727
Any benefit of health insurance
that you are able to view today.

00:09:29.752 --> 00:09:31.865
